#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗    §2  ʜᴏɴᴇʏ ᴛʜᴇ ʙᴇᴇ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝§2
Let me tell you a lovely tale about Fern’s best friend, the bee! Fern’s hair was full of flowers & had many insects come and go, but only one decided to stay. That was Honey, the resident bumblebee. They played games 
#- §2together, sang songs by the campfire, helped pollinate the local flowers and foliage and even….
§d
§kitiswatchingitiswatching
§0§5The often silent witch spoke. She muttered under her breath “what is…ɨȶ?”. Soon after, the sky turned deep purple and
began to rain ash.
#- §5The villagers froze in fear when they felt a burst of energy under their feet and heard a huge bang in the distance. Not long after they heard a rustle in the bushes behind them. They all turned to see Fern, out of breath, sword in hand. “§2I’m so sorry, but I’m going to fix this, I promise§5”.
#- §5A few minutes before, Fern was happily playing in the forest when she heard a distant but very obvious explosion of some kind. It made the ground grumble and trees tremble. Surely a coincidence that merely a moment ago she’d obtained a bewitching-looking sword, that was stuck
#- §5tightly inside an ancient-looking stone, and now was proudly holding it after several hours of determination. When held it had a faint vibration like it had a heartbeat. A dark green shimmering eye of ender was in the handle, not that Fern knew what those were at the time.
#- §6       /|§7____________ §8§7O|===|§2⏼§ §7>___________§7>
       §6\|

§5The eye slowly faded and cracked once released from the stone prison. 

Engraved on the blade was an assortment of carvings roughly translated as:
#- 
§8Property of §5ɨȶ§8. If removed, you have successfully released the soul of §5ɨȶ§8, and you have doomed us all. You are the only thing that can stop §5ɨȶ§8. Good luck. Best wishes, 

      ⚜§2The Order§8⚜ 
  ⚜§2Of The Spyglass§8⚜
#- §5Fern had no idea what the markings meant but felt a wave of fear wash over her as the sky above changed. She ran back to the village so fast that some of her petals fell off and the resident bee that lived in her hair (named Honey) was left floating in mid-air. He buzzed in anger
#- §5then casually made his way back using the trail of petals as a guide.

Fern showed the witch what she had found. Fern’s mother had never been so active and verbal. Pacing back and forth talking to herself with the occasional break to take a few deep

#- §5breaths. "§6Do you realise what you have done?§5” Fern looked up with innocent eyes and calmly said “§2umm…judging by the loud noise, the sky and your reaction... something bad I assume§5”. “§6BAD!?§
 You’ve only gone and released a powerful ancient benevolent entity, that I've only
#- §6ever been told stories of as a child myself§5” sarcastically exclaimed the witch. 

“§2In my defence, I found it in the forest, in plain sight, practically in our back garden, and if that does not scream ‘§otake me out§0§2', I don’t know what else could”. §5The witch sat down.
#- §5“§6My dear Fern, this sword was heavily enchanted to only ever present itself to those who can defeat whatever is trapped inside§5”. Thunder echoed above. “§6The Order Of The Spyglass always knew one day this would happen, but never here, not now, not you§5”.
#- §5Lightning followed almost hitting Fern but the witch grabbed it with ease from the air with her bare hands letting it melt away. 

“ɨȶ §6will never stop following you and you will never stop following §5ɨȶ”. 

Fern gulped. “§2So how do I stop §5ɨȶ§2?” 
#- §5The witch firmly took the hands of the young girl now burdened with destiny. 
“§6You find §5ɨȶ§6, 
before §5ɨȶ§6 finds you§5”. 
§d
§kitiswatchingitiswatching
§2§§And Honey the bee and Fern lived happily ever after. The end!

§6........hang on? WHAT?!?!?
#- §2To be continued…
§5✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿

