§9 A guide for making a        house a home!
#-   §9⛏*⋆§1Article Three§9⋆*⛏
   §4ᴬ ᴮⁱᵍ ᶠⁱˢʰ ᴵⁿ ᴬ ˢᵐᵃˡˡ ᴾᵒⁿᵈ
§8-------------------
§1Today, I'm sharing a few tips about making ponds/lakes or any body of water more special. I know that sounds dull, but adding life to the bland water we have can once again, dramatically change the atmosphere and
#- §1your build. 

Landscaping shouldn't be overlooked! Here are some of my personal go-to's when it comes to water.

§91. §1I like to add coarse dirt or podzol to the bottom layer to make it feel like it's dirty and podzol (depending on your texture pack)
#- §1can give the impression of tiny stones & leaves at the bottom.

§92. §1Other details for the lower areas are seagrass, coral and kelp which will add some green plant life and colour and some small animations that are more appealing to the eyes.   
#- §93. §1Getting higher up, adding living creatures such as fish, axolotls and turtles will again add moving details and make the area more believable.
                   §2 __
          .,-;-;-,. /'_\
        /_/_|_\\) /
    '-<_><_><_>=/\
     `/_/==/_/-'\_\
      ""     ""      ""
#- §94. §1The surface has potential as well by scattering lilypads on the top. I like to add cobblestone slabs around the water's edge and placed under the water in random spots to act as rocks and more detail.

§95. §1The finishing touches can be the   
#- §1odd sugarcane, mushroom, flowers and other nature placed near it. Water = Life! Also, sea pickles can light up the area so you can see all your hard work. Some player heads like the wee little froggies are adorable to place on a big dripleaf. And I can never help myself from dropping a boat
#- §1on top to create the feeling that people use the place for fishing or relaxing.

§96. §1If the area is big enough I like to add stepping stones from wooden or stone slabs or a propper bridge to get across it. Little seats or viewing platforms are also a cute addition. 
#- §8-------------------
§9⛏§1Join me next time for more Crafty Witches!§9⛏
